---
layout: changelog
title: Send push notifications without Firebase with Appwrite Push
date: 2026-10-16
cover: /images/blog/announcing-appwrite-push/cover.avif
tags: messaging, sdk
---

[Appwrite Push](/docs/products/messaging/appwrite-push) is a new push provider in Appwrite Messaging that delivers notifications without Firebase. Sending through FCM means creating a Firebase project, uploading its service account key, and collecting a device token from every install before the first message goes out. With Appwrite Push, you create the provider in the Console without any credentials, your app subscribes with the Appwrite SDK, and the messages you send from the Console or your server arrive on the device.

Messages sent to a user reach all their connected devices, and missed messages are replayed for up to 7 days. On Android the SDK keeps delivering while the app is closed, and on iOS it works with APNs and a Notification Service Extension to show messages while the app is suspended.

Push ships in Web 29.0.0, Flutter 28.0.0, React Native 2.0.0, Android 30.0.0, and Apple 21.0.0.

